  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **The Best Ever Death Metal Band In Denton** (1 review): Audience recognized this track, though the album was not yet released [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Going To Bolivia**: rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **Star Dusting**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Going To Monaco**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **The Water Song**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Born Ready**: rare: 5 archived performances [3]\n- **Going To Bristol**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Aisles**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Going To Bridlington**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Source Decay, Alphonse Mambo, Island Garden Song, The Best Ever Death Metal Band In Denton [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2001-04-21.aud.192mp3** (recommended): audience recording; 24 songs; 77 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Audio quality is poor, with the singer sounding distant and noisy [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Performance included early versions from the album All Hail West Texas [2]",
